// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: USB Storage Service Disabled Via Registry
// Sigma ID: 24e9f7a6-4fb6-4f75-b43f-c53adee748cd
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-08-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects when the USBSTOR service is disabled via the registry by setting its Start value to 4
//   (disabled). Malware uses this to prevent USB storage devices from being mounted, which stops
//   defenders from introducing recovery tools or bootable media via USB, and prevents potential data
//   exfiltration paths from being used.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative hardening policies that disable USB storage on corporate endpoints
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Siradankullanici/OpenSourceViruses/blob/3267564a35f6e13559a3119eb68d0da8d2e91a0a/suspiciousregchangesandtaskkils
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e6fa05ce10d4092a1de7d7380da240a34a30b555/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_disable_usb_storage.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\USBSTOR\\Start" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000004)"
